{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,260p' docs/AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,220p' RULES.md && sed -n '1,160p' docs/GOAL.md && git status --short --branch && git log --oneline -8 && gh issue view 36 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,body,labels,comments\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\nSame readability issue as the chords track (fixed in #21): the `[vgt] Beats` track is created muted (`add_locked_muted_track` → `B_MUTE = 1` in `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`), which renders dark-on-dark and makes its beat markers hard to read. The track carries only markers (no audio), so muting serves no audio purpose — unmuting is purely a visibility fix.\\n\\nThis resolves the open question left in #21 (\\\"leave Beats muted, or unmute it too?\\\"): **unmute it too.**\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nCreate the `[vgt] Beats` track **unmuted**. Reuse whatever unmuted-track path #21 introduced for chords (e.g. the unmuted variant/parameter of `add_locked_muted_track`).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- After apply, `[vgt] Beats` is unmuted and its markers are readable.\\n- No audio behavior change (the track has none); re-apply stays idempotent.\\n- Non-destructive; only `[vgt]`-owned objects touched.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nFollow-up to #21 (unmuted the chords track for the same reason).\",\"comments\":[],\"labels\":[{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEnfA\",\"name\":\"status:working\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"1d76db\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEoHw\",\"name\":\"implementer:codex\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"0052cc\"},{\"id\":\"LA_kwDOTcQqas8AAAACsQEo6Q\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\",\"description\":\"\",\"color\":\"fbca04\"}],\"number\":36,\"title\":\"Unmute the [vgt] Beats track so its beat markers are readable\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
