6-\nREADME.md:187:**Chords**: edit items directly on the `[vgt] Chords` track's timeline — its\nREADME.md-188-items are unlocked (though still muted, so they never play):\nREADME.md-189-\nREADME.md-190-- **rename** an item's take to relabel a chord (e.g. `Am` → `A`);\nREADME.md-191-- **move or resize** an item to adjust its boundaries;\nREADME.md-192-- **split** an item (REAPER's native split action) to break one chord into two;\n--\nREADME.md-199-When done with either (or both), load\nREADME.md-200-[reascript/vgt_sync.lua](reascript/vgt_sync.lua) in REAPER's Action List and\nREADME.md-201-run it (or run `vgt sync [project.rpp]` for the same pointer from the CLI).\nREADME.md-202-It:\nREADME.md-203-\nREADME.md:204:- scans the `[vgt] Chords` track's items — position, length, take name — by\nREADME.md-205-  GUID against the sidecar's `managed_track_guids`, so it only ever reads a\nREADME.md-206-  chords track vgt itself created, and writes them back as\nREADME.md-207-  `analysis.chords.value.segments` with `chords.human_verified: true`;\nREADME.md-208-- scans regions by ID against the sidecar's `managed_region_ids`, never any\nREADME.md-209-  other project region (including a user region whose name starts with\n--\nREADME.md-213-  the original machine detections stay available there (#19) — nor any other\nREADME.md-214-  analysis stage (tempo, key) or the rest of the sidecar.\nREADME.md-215-\nREADME.md-216-From then on: `vgt analyze` skips the chords and sections stages\nREADME.md-217-(human-verified stages are never recomputed), and re-running the apply\nREADME.md:218:ReaScript repaints `[vgt] Chords` and the section regions identically from\nREADME.md-219-the corrected sidecar — the round trip is idempotent.\nREADME.md-220-\nREADME.md-221-## Check vgt state\nREADME.md-222-\nREADME.md-223-`vgt status [project.rpp]` is read-only: it prints the project and sidecar,\n--\nreascript/vgt_initialize.lua-329-  reaper.GetSetMediaItemInfo_String(item, \"P_NOTES\", label, true)\